\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par   1.\cf0   O! Thou guarantor and everlasting priest
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj    Thou who was hanged, our great Redeemer
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0    Sinners as we are, you were pleading for
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj    before you died for the whole of mankind
\par    If I know how to say a genuine prayer
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0    be my advocate and plead on for me
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   2.  Thou deserve our thanks because of Thy love
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj    How you spoke to console your mother,
\par    and to her care your beloved servant
\par    for the compassion that you had for her
\par    Jesus, you loved your people to the end
\par     Take care of me also and my kingsmen too.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   3.  You deserve thanks for your comforting words
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0    with which you assured the sinner man
\par   And thus you opened the heaven's door for him
\par   though our sins have imprisoned us here
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj   Make merry! You sinners and be happy
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj The Word is the Key to Paradise.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Blessed art Thou, that during your struggle
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj  You, with a loud voice shouted out and said
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0  My God! My God! Why hast thou forsaken me.
\par Tis me, tis me said so to your father
\par  Jesus, I'll look to this ever and always
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj  My God won't reject me though I stand accused.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Jesus, the Lord of the heav'ns we give thanks
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj the bitter wine you were given to take
\par when you were hanged on the cross and thirsty
\par so I drink from your life giving fountain
\par  I shall no more fear the fire of satan
\par  Jesus thou hast conquered satan by your death
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.\cf0  Thank you because the word has been fulfilled
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj When you screamed out and said, "It is finished"
\par Because of our death and for our atonement
\par You offered yourself as a sacrifice
\par To pacify God and erased all our sins
\par And your holy blood is pleading for us now.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. You deserve our thanks as in your suff'ring
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj Op'd out your mouth, gave up your spirit too
\par Through what we received life-long and blessing
\par And fully paid the price completely.
\par We wholly give our spirits and soul to you
\par From our death time and to all eternity.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-360\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   8. Jesus it is my will to die with you
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj Jesus, that I shall resurrect with you
\par Jesus, that I shall reign with you in heaven
\par Jesus, so I shall take my rest with you
\par Jesus, so I eternally with you rest
\par \pard         Jesus, you the Amen, thine for evermore\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

